 ar flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelin
 es:\n•  Handle costume pieces with care while changing to prevent d
 amage to delicate fabrics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in th
 e event of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how sign
 ificant\n•  Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or h
 ang costumes by their elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sitting on th
 e floor while in costume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean
 \, or launder any costume or accessory\n•  Never apply stage make-u
 p while in costume and shall take great care to refrain from smudging ma
 ke-up on costume during its removal\n•  Refrain from the use of spr
 ay perfume or cologne while in costume\n•  Never wear any garment n
 ot assigned to cast member\n•  Do not handle or consume food or bev
 erage while in costume\, with the exception of water\n•  Do not rem
 ove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n•
   Remove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following
  their use\n•  Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n• 
  Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe
  policies\n•  Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anyt
 hing that may damage or stain costumes.
